  "order": 10,
  "accent": "signal",
  "recommendedHours": 95,
  "description": "Programming from first principles in C: precise control flow, data representation, functions, arrays, pointers, compilation, debugging and the beginnings of a machine-level mental model.",
  "prerequisites": [],
  "outcomes": [
    "Write, compile, test and debug non-trivial C programs without relying on framework abstractions.",
    "Reason about objects, addresses, arrays, strings, pointers and function calls with a concrete memory model.",
    "Use decomposition, invariants and defensive input handling to turn problem statements into reliable programs.",
    "Read compiler diagnostics and debugger state rather than treating errors as opaque failures.",
    "Explain the boundary between source code, compiler, linker, executable and process."
  ],
